- The length of the integer array parameter `digits` is less than or equal to 100 and is greater than or equal to 1.
- All the values in the integer array parameter `digits` are less than or equal to 9 and are greater than or equal to 0.
- The length of the integer array result is equal to the length of the integer array parameter `digits`.
- The integer array result represents the large integer obtained by incrementing the integer array parameter `digits` by one.
- If the last element of the integer array parameter `digits` is less than 9, the last element of the integer array result is equal to the last element of the integer array parameter `digits` plus 1.
- If the last element of the integer array parameter `digits` is equal to 9, the last element of the integer array result is equal to 0 and the second last element of the integer array result is equal to the second last element of the integer array parameter `digits` plus 1.
- If all elements of the integer array parameter `digits` are equal to 9, the first element of the integer array result is equal to 1 and all other elements are equal to 0.